# 395 — R-177 batch 7 (D-144): GREEN — in-process resource sampler, leak indicators, root cause of fds=0

## 1. root cause of fds=0 in the log-390 soak (PROVEN, reproduced here)
server.py:80 calls safety.harden_server_process() = prctl(PR_SET_DUMPABLE, 0) (R-100 security control).
A non-dumpable process's /proc/<pid>/fd and smaps_rollup are owned by root and unreadable (EACCES) to every
other process of the same user, INCLUDING its parent. status/stat stay mode 0444, so RSS/threads were
measurable and fds were not. The old sidecar 'ls /proc/$pid/fd 2>/dev/null | wc -l' hid the error and printed 0.
The earlier hypothesis about the '<' (high priority) STAT flag is NOT the cause and is withdrawn.
Live reproduction on this sandbox (same command as the codespace soak, then via the launcher):
