## 2. fix (hardening NOT disabled)
- scripts/r177_sut_launcher.py: equivalent to 'python -m uvicorn server:app --port P' (cwd first on sys.path, same
  uvicorn entry point); when R177_RES_CSV is set it starts ONE daemon thread inside the SUT that samples its own /proc
  (a process may always read its own entries). Cost: one small /proc read per tick (soak 10s, other profiles 1s).
- scripts/r177_resource_sampler.py: count_fds -> None + errno reason on failure, NEVER 0; read_sample (VmRSS, VmHWM,
  Threads, Pss, Private_Dirty, Anonymous, utime, stime, fds); OLS slope/h + 95% CI after a warm-up cut (max(25%, 600s));
  growth_significant = CI lower bound > 0. Indicator only: no approved leak threshold exists (proposed), no 'no leak' claim.
- scripts/r177_per_service.py: report['resources'] = {in_process (authoritative), external (cross-check, PermissionError
  recorded), leak_indicators, leak_indicators_source}; --failure-recovery now honours --service (default unchanged:
  api-tasks-submit); failure_recovery result gains resources_during/resources_post and a descriptive 'outcome'
  (stopped_and_recovered | unaffected_no_stop | failed). ok semantics are UNCHANGED (a fault no stop rule caught stays ok=False).
- thresholds, profiles, SLOs, stop limits: unchanged. server.py: unchanged.

